From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0371-mario-03-gpu-only-regions-unwritten.patch

Source: 0371-mario-03-gpu-only-regions-unwritten.patch
Core patch: goes in tools/eglantine-patches as 0183-... (after 0182). Paths are the submodule's.

nx2.h follows which blocks were written for sparse regions only. For a GPU-only region backed as
it is written, Nx2SparseBlockIsWritten answers "written", because it does not know the region. Two
things follow, both read from the source:
- BackSparseWrite's rule that zeros over an empty block need no memory never applies there.
- IsUnwrittenSparse never applies there. Mario Kart World's 8192x8192 RG16 image at 0x85f5fb0000
  (341 MiB) and its 3072x3072x2 at 0x81783f0000 (96 MiB) are GPU-only and held whole, flags 0x70
  in runs 45 and 52: not marked GPU-written at the end. None of the sparse images of that shape
  reaches the top ten of the refusal report (under 36 MiB each).

EDEN_NX2_GPU_ONLY_UNWRITTEN=1 (off unless set) has nx2.h follow those regions too. Zeros over a
block nobody wrote then take none, and a colour texture of 32 MiB or more with mip levels over such
blocks gets no memory until a write, by the path sparse regions use. Render targets have one level
and are left alone: the first draw into such an image is lost. Sparse layers and tiles do not see
these regions (Nx2InSparseRegion stays false).

"Nobody wrote" has to count the GPU here, and a GPU-only region holds render targets whose contents
never reach a block. So PrepareImage marks the region's blocks written at an image's first GPU
write (the GPU-modified flag going on, not every draw). Without that, a mip-mapped texture joined
over a render target came up unbacked and CopyImage dropped the target's contents. It only touches
regions flagged gpu_only: with the switch off there are none and nothing changes.

Ocarina of Time cannot be affected: LazyGpuOnlyRegions is false for it, so it has no such regions.

Always on, logging only: one line for each region's first block, saying what the write held, and
the every-64-blocks line now counts blocks taken by zeros and names the block. Runs 45 and 52 back
1021 MiB in 0.6 s at the same point; this says where and whether it was zeros.

Guess: whether those two images are unwritten when they are made, and whether that burst is zeros.
If they are written, this saves nothing and changes nothing. A region is GPU-only because the GPU
writes it, so expect the saving to end at the first such write: that draw or compute pass is lost
and the image comes back backed (the log says "GPU write into unwritten sparse image"). A texture
drawn into once would stay empty.

Checked on a Mac, not on the console: a host test of nx2.h; the generated vk_texture_cache_cost.cpp,
vk_texture_cache_base.cpp (the template) and nx2_gsv.h (through self_controller.cpp) pass clang
-fsyntax-only with stub headers. tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py reports the same two anchors with and
without this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

